title: $:/plugins/BTC/PrintRiver/usage

!! Overview

''PrintRiver'' opens a dedicated print window that renders a configurable story river — giving you full control over which tiddlers to print, their order, and how the printed page looks.

!! Getting started

# Open the print window by clicking the ''Print'' button (🖨) in any tiddler's toolbar.
# The print window shows the tiddlers in `$:/PrintList`.
# Use the toolbar at the top of the print window to adjust layout and content before printing.
# Click the ''Print'' button (🖨) in the print-window toolbar to send to the printer.

!! Print-window toolbar

|!Button |!What it does |
|☰ (sort) |Reorder or remove tiddlers in the print list by drag-and-drop. |
|🖨 (print) |Trigger the browser print dialog. |
|⬇ (export LaTeX) |Download the current print list as a compilable `.tex` file. |
|⚙ (tools) |Open the tools panel to adjust fonts, line-height, header/footer settings, and LaTeX options. |

!! Header & Footer

Each printed page can have text in up to six margin positions.  Configure them in the ''Tools → Header/Footer'' panel.

!!! Content tokens

Use these tokens anywhere in a header or footer field:

|!Token |!Replaced with |!Example output |
|`<<date>>` |Current date at print time |`02 Mar 2026` |
|`<<time>>` |Current time (12-hour, AM/PM) |`9:05 AM` |
|`<<page>>` |Current page number |`3` |
|`<<pages>>` |Total number of pages |`5` |

Tokens can be combined with plain text, e.g. `Page <<page>> of <<pages>>`.

!!! Positions & defaults

|!Config tiddler |!Position |!Default value |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-left` |Top-left of every page |`<<date>> <<time>>` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-center` |Top-centre of every page |`TiddlyWiki5 - PrintRiver` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-right` |Top-right of every page |''(empty)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/footer-left` |Bottom-left of every page |''(empty)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/footer-center` |Bottom-centre of every page |''(empty)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/footer-right` |Bottom-right of every page |`<<page>>/<<pages>>` |

> ''Note:'' Disable the browser's built-in "Headers and footers" option in the print dialog to avoid overlap with these CSS margin-box settings.

!!! Header & Footer Style

A single set of style settings applies to all six positions.  Leave any field empty to inherit the browser default.

|!Config tiddler |!CSS property |!Example value |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-footer-fontsize` |`font-size` |`9pt`, `11px`, `0.8em` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-footer-fontfamily` |`font-family` |`Arial, sans-serif`, `Georgia, serif` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-footer-color` |`color` |`#555`, `gray`, `darkblue` |

!! River-level typography

These settings apply to the entire print story river (all tiddlers).

|!Config tiddler |!CSS property |!Example value |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/fontsize` |`font-size` |`12pt`, `14px`, `1em` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/lineheight` |`line-height` |`1.5`, `1.8`, `24px` |

!! Tiddler body typography

These settings apply only to the body text inside each tiddler, overriding the river-level values.

|!Config tiddler |!CSS property |!Example value |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/tiddler-body-fontsize` |`font-size` |`11pt`, `13px` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/tiddler-body-lineheight` |`line-height` |`1.6`, `22px` |

!! Per-tiddler controls

Each tiddler in the print window has a small control bar.  Toggle:

|!Control |!What it does |
|title |Show or hide the tiddler title. |
|subtitle |Show or hide the tiddler subtitle. |
|tags |Show or hide the tiddler tags. |
|text |Center-align the tiddler body text. |
|break |Insert a page break before this tiddler. |

!! Complete config tiddler reference

|!Config tiddler |!Purpose |!Default |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/fontsize` |River font size |''(browser default)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/lineheight` |River line height |''(browser default)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/tiddler-body-fontsize` |Tiddler body font size |''(browser default)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/tiddler-body-lineheight` |Tiddler body line height |''(browser default)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-left` |Header left content |`<<date>> <<time>>` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-center` |Header centre content |`TiddlyWiki5 - PrintRiver` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-right` |Header right content |''(empty)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/footer-left` |Footer left content |''(empty)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/footer-center` |Footer centre content |''(empty)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/footer-right` |Footer right content |`<<page>>/<<pages>>` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-footer-fontsize` |Header/footer font size |''(browser default)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-footer-fontfamily` |Header/footer font family |''(browser default)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/header-footer-color` |Header/footer text colour |''(browser default)'' |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-documentclass` |LaTeX document class |`article` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-paper` |LaTeX paper size option |`a4paper` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-fontsize` |LaTeX base font size |`11pt` |
|`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-extra-preamble` |Custom LaTeX preamble commands |''(empty)'' |

!! LaTeX Export

Click the ''Export LaTeX'' button (⬇) in the print-window toolbar to download a compilable `.tex` file containing all tiddlers in the print list.

!!! What gets converted

|!Content |!LaTeX output |
|Headings (`!`, `!!`, …) |`\section`, `\subsection`, `\subsubsection`, … |
|Bold / italic / underline / strikethrough |`\textbf`, `\textit`, `\underline`, `\sout` |
|Inline code / code blocks |`\texttt{}` / `verbatim` environment |
|Bullet and numbered lists |`itemize` / `enumerate` environments |
|Tables |`tabular` environment wrapped in `table` float |
|`<figure>` elements / `<img>` tags |`figure` environment with `\includegraphics` |
|KaTeX/MathJax inline math |`$…$` (annotation extracted from rendered HTML) |
|KaTeX/MathJax display math with `\label{}` |`equation` environment (numbered) |
|KaTeX/MathJax display math without `\label{}` |`\[…\]` (unnumbered) |
|Pre-existing `\begin{align}` / `equation` blocks |Passed through as-is |
|Mermaid diagrams |`tikzpicture` stub; mermaid source preserved as comments |
|Links to tiddlers in the print list |`\hyperref[sec:…]{…}` cross-references |
|Links to tiddlers not in the print list |Plain text + `\footnote{Tiddler: …}` |
|External URLs |`\href{url}{text}` |

!!! Equation labels

To produce a numbered equation, include a `\label{eq:…}` command inside the display-math delimiters of your tiddler, e.g.:

```
$$\label{eq:energy} E = mc^2$$
```

This will export as:

```latex
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:energy} E = mc^2
\end{equation}
```

!!! Mermaid → TikZ

Mermaid diagrams are exported as empty `tikzpicture` environments with the original mermaid source preserved in comments.  Replace the stub with the equivalent TikZ code to include diagrams in the compiled PDF.

!!! LaTeX settings (Tools panel)

Open the ⚙ ''Tools'' menu and scroll to ''LaTeX Export Settings'' to configure:

|!Setting |!Config tiddler |!Default |
|Document class |`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-documentclass` |`article` |
|Paper size |`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-paper` |`a4paper` |
|Font size |`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-fontsize` |`11pt` |
|Extra preamble |`$:/config/PrintRiver/latex-extra-preamble` |''(empty)'' |

> ''Note:'' Valid document classes are `article`, `report`, and `book`.  For `book` and `report`, top-level tiddlers are mapped to `\chapter` rather than `\section`.

!!! Compiling the exported file

The downloaded `.tex` file requires a standard LaTeX installation (e.g. TeX Live or MiKTeX).  Compile with:

```
pdflatex tiddlers-export.tex
pdflatex tiddlers-export.tex   # run twice for cross-references
```
